codex
The loop theorem remains solid and closes over an arbitrary untouched scope remainder. To avoid relying on an unproved summary rule, I’m expressing the end-to-end proof as two composable reachability claims: a finite public-entry prefix that reaches the initialized loop head, and the already-proved loop suffix that returns the mathematical largest proper divisor. This keeps every proof step checked by `kprove` without trusting a sibling claim.
